{"duration_api_ms":82122,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0adaf74f-6d73-4d30-b323-cf27df0720a6","total_cost_usd":0.297767,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16713,"cache_read_input_tokens":105115,"output_tokens":7150,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2948},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16713,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4172,"cache_read_input_tokens":27739,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2252},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":7150,"cacheReadInputTokens":105115,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16713,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.297767,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2948,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"reject\",\n  \"diff_digest\": \"309e90a576905974178f8ebcb40a6d2c78a69f6c70ac76e5ee3b55a57c4f1aa0\",\n  \"violations\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": 28,\n      \"location\": \"external/ccbench/cc/silo/transaction.cc: TxExecutor::read_internal, in the loop that rechecks the TID word (stock lines 270-277; the working diff hunk is labelled @@ -401 and adds `break;` right after `expected = check;`)\",\n      \"correctness_impact\": \"In stock code, the value is copied (263) and then the TID word is read again (270). If the word changed, the loop retries. With `break;` added right after `expected = check;`, a mismatch exits the loop anyway, and read_set_.emplace_back(..., body, expected) at 277 files the value together with the new version (check). The value came from the old version, or is a torn mix of old and new bytes caught partway through writePhase. The read set now claims 'I read version v_new' while holding a value that belongs to no version. Validation at 453-454 only compares epoch/tid against this recorded check, so if nobody writes afterwards it passes and the transaction commits. Example: T reads x while writer W changes x from 5 to 6 and publishes v_new. T gets the value 5 but records version v_new, writes 5+1=6 as v_next, and commits. W's update is lost, so the history is not serializable. The skipped retry also skips the absent check at 260: a key deleted in between can return OK with the pre-delete value, and an absent word goes into the read set. Q1 (which version a read returns), Q3 (version identifier), Q8 (intermediate values) and Q5 (delete) all break.\",\n      \"verifier_blind_spot\": \"The trace R line is emitted from read_set_'s re.get_tidword() (stock line 607), so it carries the version recorded as check, the new one. The version-level dependency graph reads 'T read v_new and wrote v_next', a serial order, and finds no G2 cycle. The value is not in the trace, so version-level checks cannot see the gap between version and value (a torn read). Only the value stamp comparison (semantic version 2 Q/V lines) can see it, and it only fires if the workload makes the tuple overwrite race with the re-read of the TID word. On workloads without that race, verification comes back green without having tested anything.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": 13,\n      \"location\": \"external/ccbench/cc/silo/transaction.cc: TxExecutor::read_internal (the whole working diff)\",\n      \"correctness_impact\": \"This axis only lets the candidate edit the hole between `EVOLVE-BLOCK-BEGIN/END silo-lock-order-policy` (patched lines 46-55: the bodies of order_enabled, order_priority, order_after_abort, order_on_commit). This diff does not touch that hole at all; it rewrites the consistent-read protocol in the read path, which is skeleton code. transaction.cc is editable at file granularity, so the hook cannot stop this; it has to be rejected at line level. Under the axis framing ('decide the lock order in validation by priority'), it swaps in a behavior change that has nothing to do with lock order.\",\n      \"verifier_blind_spot\": \"The verifier only checks the trace after commit. It does not check which lines a diff touches. The trace also has no field that shows the read loop was cut short.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": 30,\n      \"location\": \"The working diff as a whole vs. mechanism_spec.rules R1-R8 / q_declarations\",\n      \"correctness_impact\": \"(a) The one changed line (the `break;` in read_internal) is not the implementation of any rule R1-R8, all of which cover lock order, priority computation, no-wait, and validation order. It is behavior outside the rules. Conversely, the rules are carried by skeleton code in the patch (R1: sort_write_set's INSERT/DELETE check and stock sort; R2: the comparator; R3: the read_word lambda; R6: lockWriteSet's NO_WAIT branch; R7: the order inside validationPhase). The hole still holds the stub (order_enabled=false), so this diff implements no rule. (b) Q1-Q8 are all declared unchanged, but independent answers from the code disagree.\",\n      \"verifier_blind_spot\": \"The small-model check covers the specification (lock-order permutations), not the read path. 'No counterexample in the registered range' says nothing about whether the implementation matches the spec. The verifier cannot see the Q declarations either.\",\n      \"note\": \"Q1: declared=unchanged independent=changes; Q3: declared=unchanged independent=changes; Q8: declared=unchanged independent=changes; Q5: declared=unchanged independent=changes (skipping the absent check lets a deleted record be read as OK); Q2: declared=unchanged independent=undetermined (can the value from partway through writePhase, which the loop now exits with, be treated as the value of a transaction that has not committed yet? That depends on where the commit point is, and I did not settle it)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nits\": [\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"With `break;` added, the `++result_->local_extra_reads_` under `#if ADD_ANALYSIS` can never run (dead code), and the `for (;;)` is no longer really a loop (only the lock spin at 255 remains).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tests\": [\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"Apply this exact diff (insert `break;` right after `expected = check;` in read_internal) as the break patch. Workload: 1 hot key, all threads doing read-modify-write (+1), with a short sleep inserted in the TRACE build between copying the value and re-reading the TID word, to force the race.\",\n      \"expected_gate\": \"reject (the value stamp comparison, semantic version 2 Q/V lines, shows a mismatch between the recorded version and the value's stamp; also, the final value != initial value + number of committed increments)\",\n      \"machine_judgment\": \"The driver re-runs with this patch and treats it as red if (1) the verifier finds 1 or more mismatches where the Q/V line version and the value's stamp disagree, or (2) at run end the hot key's value minus the initial value differs from the sum of per-thread commit counts. If the stock build shows neither and this patch shows either, the control has teeth. If the patched build shows neither, record the control as having no teeth (vacuous).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"Break patch 2: remove the `if (expected.absent) return Status::WARN_NOT_FOUND;` check at line 260 in read_internal (a torn read that goes through the path where a record is deleted in between). Workload: mix delete and re-insert on a hot key with reads of it.\",\n      \"expected_gate\": \"Add a positive control assert under #if TRACE: when read_set_.emplace_back runs, expected.lock==0 and expected.absent==0 hold, and expected matches the word re-read right after copying the value. If it fails, emit a `P torn-read` line. The verifier maps P lines to indeterminate. Both this diff and patch 2 should turn it red.\",\n      \"machine_judgment\": \"The driver counts P torn-read lines in the trace. Stock build = 0 and break patch ≥ 1 is the pass condition for the positive control (mutation_red_gate). If the break patch also gives 0, record the assert as a no-op (type 1/11). The assert is not a no-op only if, in the break patch, the value copy and the word re-read happen at different times.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"mutation\": \"Small-model risky versions, one broken rule each: R1 = a candidate order even for write sets that include INSERT/DELETE; R2 = the candidate returns the full order itself (storage/key tie-breaks removed); R3 = the TID word re-read after sorting and passed to the candidate; R4 = the candidate references read_set_/write_set_/result_; R5 = sorting drops or duplicates elements; R6 = lock waits instead of no-wait, or prior locks are not released on conflict; R7 = validation before all locks are taken, or writes before validation; R8 = priority uses locked.\",\n      \"expected_gate\": \"Each version should produce a counterexample (cc-model-counterexample/1, with rule_ids naming that rule). R6's liveness side and the INSERT/DELETE case for R1 are out_of_scope for the current model, so they must be registered as scenarios first.\",\n      \"machine_judgment\": \"The small-model checker's output must have result=counterexample and rule_ids containing the target rule. If no counterexample appears in the registered range, record that rule's check as vacuous (type 1).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainty\": \"(1) The working diff's hunk label (@@ -401) does not match the position in the designated stock transaction.cc (270-272) plus the patch offset (about +125, so about 395). I identified the location from the context lines, which match one place in the file (`if (expected == check) break;` occurs only at line 271), but I did not check whether git apply lands it exactly there. (2) abort_digest is empty, so I cannot check whether this branch ran during verification or whether the race was hit (type 4/26). (3) The model_check_summary digest matches mechanism_spec and the result is no-counterexample, so there is no input defect. But the check does not cover the read path, so the result gives no support for the correctness of this change. (4) Whether Q2 changes (whether the torn value counts as 'the value of an uncommitted transaction') is undetermined. (5) I opened no files containing fitness, throughput, or runs/wal.jsonl.\"\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1824,"type":"result","duration_ms":102287,"uuid":"679ed700-f116-49d3-9b98-c8e030d76631","ttft_stream_ms":1516,"time_to_request_ms":58,"first_content_frame_ms":1517,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
